    "done_when": "tests/test_a_wait_no_sweep_can_lift_reaches_its_coordinator.py, on a temporary crew home, holds a live pointer in phase working whose recorded pids are dead and whose manifest reads status: waiting with wait_condition, wait_terminal, wait_expected: 1h and resume_brief but no wait_probe or wait_file, declared 13 h before the test's clock. The test asserts the owning session's obligation view holds exactly one row for the run, that the row's text names wait_probe, and that its suggested command is reckon crew resume --run followed by the run's own id and --advice. A second case with a valid sacct-shaped probe that is not yet met asserts the run raises no such row. Negative control: at the base revision the first case's row names neither wait_probe nor that command, so the test fails there. The test files importing the changed modules add no failure against base in matched arms run as an all_debug partition job, submitted with env -u SLURM_JOB_ID -u SLURM_JOBID sbatch and never on the fleet node. Each arm's log sits under the run directory, opens with its revision and literal command, and ends in EXIT=. The gate command is relative and literal (PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q tests/test_a_wait_no_sweep_can_lift_reaches_its_coordinator.py), and names no worktree path. ruff check and ruff format --check add no finding on the staged paths.",
